Package: wavetune
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: @ARCH@
Maintainer: onlymash <fiepi.dev@gmail.com>
Installed-Size: @INSTALLED_SIZE@
Depends: libc6, libgcc-s1, libgtk-4-1 (>= 4.10), libadwaita-1-0 (>= 1.9), libbluetooth3, libdbus-1-3, libwebp7, bluez
Suggests: gnome-shell (>= 45)
Section: sound
Priority: optional
Homepage: https://github.com/onlymash/WaveTune
Description: Unofficial multi-brand wireless headset control center
 WaveTune is an unofficial control center for multi-brand wireless headsets
 on Linux (ported from EncoDeck), built with GTK4 and libadwaita. It currently
 supports OPPO, OnePlus, and realme, with future support planned for Huawei,
 Xiaomi, Vivo, and Edifier. It reads battery, firmware, and wear state and can
 change noise-control modes on supported models over Bluetooth.
 .
 This project is not affiliated with or endorsed by any vendor.
